1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,078
ShadeRoute is a mobile-first walking planner for people who need to reduce direct-sun exposure.

2
00:00:06,078 --> 00:00:12,852
It is designed for heat-vulnerable people and carers, and for frontline or outdoor workers making repeated journeys.

3
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:21,618
In the next two minutes, I’ll show how someone plans a route, compares the trade-off and watches shade move through the day.

4
00:00:22,918 --> 00:00:26,800
The problem is not simply finding the shortest walk.

5
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:34,564
Two alternatives can take roughly the same time but pass through different street canyons, open spaces and shadows.

6
00:00:34,564 --> 00:00:38,446
ShadeRoute puts that exposure trade-off next to travel time.

7
00:00:38,446 --> 00:00:47,936
The current prototype focuses on two hospital corridors, where journeys may be repeated and where clarity matters more than a black-box recommendation.

8
00:00:49,236 --> 00:00:51,469
The workflow is deliberately familiar.

9
00:00:51,469 --> 00:01:00,852
First, enter the start and destination, choose a result, use the current location, or place an exact point on the map.

10
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:04,872
Second, set the London departure time and journey needs.

11
00:01:04,872 --> 00:01:08,447
Third, compare up to three real walking alternatives.

12
00:01:08,447 --> 00:01:16,042
ShadeRoute never treats unconfirmed text as a location, and custom points remain inside the selected pilot area.

13
00:01:17,342 --> 00:01:19,038
This is the centrepiece.

14
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:27,093
The three-dimensional map uses local building and surface data, then changes the displayed shadows as the departure time moves.

15
00:01:27,093 --> 00:01:33,029
The selected route is broken into potential sun, estimated shade, uncertain and unknown sections.

16
00:01:33,029 --> 00:01:39,389
That means the visual is useful without pretending the model knows more than it does.

17
00:01:39,389 --> 00:01:44,052
The route cards remain available if three-dimensional graphics are not usable.

18
00:01:45,352 --> 00:01:57,931
Today, ShadeRoute can compare real route alternatives, replay shade through time, prepare verified offline pilot packs, save journeys on the device, and show optional heat or transport context.

19
00:01:57,931 --> 00:02:11,409
The next step is not a wider claim; it is a controlled field pilot across the two corridors, with carers and outdoor workers, and measured calibration before any stronger recommendation.

20
00:02:11,409 --> 00:02:16,351
ShadeRoute is practical now and honest about what still needs proof.
